#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119687 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "85acf106-2f03-5509-8ad0-08b82ef2a4c6" :question/math-academy-id "e-8005" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n![](images/9c/9cb26049b5e3d06f9ef9e07ce617042166330b1eddb84063d7970799ebf6d8e5.png)\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of $a_{31}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4 \\times 4$ determinant to a $3 \\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the right of $a_{31}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (or column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+3{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-3){C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -3 & -5 & 11\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -3 & -5 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -5 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -5 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(11-3) \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119690 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119874 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b0edd60-2801-59d3-b9df-18bfbf8763bb" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "4a9954b2-3d4b-5669-88cd-6e74c9683a60" :question/math-academy-id "e-8054" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Find a $3\\times 3$ determinant that has the same value.\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below $a_{11}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries below $a_{11}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (or column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -8 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -8 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 & -9 \\\\ -10 & -8 & -9 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 & -9 \\\\ -10 & -8 & -9 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119691 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "ccf558b9-bf00-58c7-b244-2c5797f93d8e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8060" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -4 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Find a $3\\times 3$ determinant that has the same value.\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of $a_{23}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of $a_{23}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (or column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -4 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 11\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266066 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119874 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b0edd60-2801-59d3-b9df-18bfbf8763bb" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "754569dc-c33c-5246-bef6-de39612bd634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -7 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264019} {:answer/id #uuid "853968c1-8cfe-5637-b142-164d9645f0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 15 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264148} {:answer/id #uuid "a34b9756-88e8-5714-ae4f-fa4f3d173d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264384} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5075fc-0c0f-5424-9ff7-b11495204153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264489} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a32961-3630-510e-b3e8-27971f2836e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -1 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a34b9756-88e8-5714-ae4f-fa4f3d173d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264384} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cad95cc-57da-561f-b114-9f218f13d2b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23bb6d19-f0bc-58f3-805e-627e1903136e" :question/math-academy-id "q-131256" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{34}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{34}=3$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 6 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 6 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{3+4}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3918d02d-79a2-5245-9ab6-bd95e4e96915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388253} {:answer/id #uuid "2c45615d-4f2b-5ac9-b5dc-e4f43dac6ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388254} {:answer/id #uuid "36c6b408-d5d5-589a-a660-9ef15feecae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388255} {:answer/id #uuid "58472625-1fbc-537b-9c8f-5e2f7ee28d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388256} {:answer/id #uuid "7d18a2b2-9593-54ad-b487-9d6b01810ddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 12 \\\\ 7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36c6b408-d5d5-589a-a660-9ef15feecae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388255} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6ab624e-b5cd-5b5e-8dbf-171c60613d15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "16ee071c-dc61-52a6-97dd-99854448ee3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-132003" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -11 & 7 & 9 & -6\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -11 & 7 & 9 & -6\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-2){C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b024a3-fa6e-5a50-9629-99ef7def6fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "462" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263154} {:answer/id #uuid "3765d51c-d5ac-519a-9e70-5cd93e1c8ff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "414" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263497} {:answer/id #uuid "6298a35d-c73e-5280-8353-3dc2e6fba29d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "298" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263849} {:answer/id #uuid "ca000009-455a-58b7-9c8d-de3f64fdc56b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "531" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264766} {:answer/id #uuid "ffbfdd21-cacf-55dc-9222-240b2a07e47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "378" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3765d51c-d5ac-519a-9e70-5cd93e1c8ff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "414" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263497} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eb1dbd9-5423-5c3a-8e04-931fffbce60e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d00f5bdf-fb0f-57e8-b395-12f0570296a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-132163" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -6 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & 10 & 12 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -8 & -2\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{11}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{11}=3$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -6 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & 10 & 12 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -8 & -2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 9 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 9 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (3)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}9 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =9(18+28) \\\\  & =9(46) \\\\  & =414.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89a9045a-7bce-5521-9e5e-c18cda1bc188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118629} {:answer/id #uuid "1428c966-b14f-5658-a6f5-11220376879d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118630} {:answer/id #uuid "2370d1bf-4d63-5ef2-82b0-1bf300a84b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118631} {:answer/id #uuid "47b9c8a5-e5a1-5b17-a0a2-47a2f155c5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118632} {:answer/id #uuid "5f193840-cca0-5ffb-95a1-ae4e4782955b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118633}] :answer-field/id #uuid "67dfd6a1-fb8e-5c81-a959-a13da9e1b424" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118628}] :question/id #uuid "150c328e-7322-5fa3-b605-dd458b140db6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42075" :question/problem "Calculate the value of\n$\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}$.\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below $a_{11}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4 \\cdot 4$ determinant to a $3 \\cdot 3$ determinant.*"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "609d4aa3-2241-5f9d-b6f4-1a30887ca390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394856} {:answer/id #uuid "30f3764a-811a-5eab-869c-ec0be3239d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394857} {:answer/id #uuid "5044ffe8-6af3-542a-b299-73a548e1de0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394858} {:answer/id #uuid "0d21572b-0d8b-5bbe-ae1d-2219314d5b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394859} {:answer/id #uuid "470fd86e-b0d9-5a17-a025-3164e11aa781" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "470fd86e-b0d9-5a17-a025-3164e11aa781" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394860} :answer-field/id #uuid "c480dcb0-6f15-525e-b469-6c0d8ba55637" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ff3ecd8-fc32-55c0-acc0-bdc23d568e06" :question/math-academy-id "q-91217" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{42}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{42}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-2){C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce668a86-7b7f-5cce-ae60-bce01ee2e316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119396} {:answer/id #uuid "d3436ed4-ae7f-59ee-85b6-f4ab5fea7c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\begin{vmatrix}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -7\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119397} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a3b912-b49a-5701-865a-ce912be6915e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119398} {:answer/id #uuid "e7216e7c-0264-5e6f-aa7e-1a96b323379a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119399} {:answer/id #uuid "f719a53b-c4a4-54a3-b429-4c86bc557fd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\begin{vmatrix}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119400}] :answer-field/id #uuid "95501011-36b6-5fb0-a872-1181bea9f135" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119395} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46cd8000-1e23-5199-b2db-301eb99e864d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394862} {:answer/id #uuid "1289a79f-f03a-57c5-80ce-7fd42973e8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394863} {:answer/id #uuid "7a2989e5-bdd3-537a-85ba-5abd1555a897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394864} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd0f37a-c44f-5c54-9e1a-bd783a206783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394865} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ae3856-08c7-541a-9fe1-12f594788fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dd0f37a-c44f-5c54-9e1a-bd783a206783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394865} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8b159e-b89f-5a64-b5d5-e5aa63c40762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2a2b160-a569-5696-8596-179bbcebb9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-91220" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-3){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-1){C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086baf34-04b6-58fc-b9f8-cd256a0f2e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354739} {:answer/id #uuid "3456bcab-7477-5733-9df3-89b18380c3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355127} {:answer/id #uuid "424cdac0-33e0-589e-94e9-d123e607def9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355250} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc929ce-9e29-5c94-bc6a-5cbf8f8914e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355906} {:answer/id #uuid "aebbe85d-89ff-5c2d-9a47-bea4603e6c6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3456bcab-7477-5733-9df3-89b18380c3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355127} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a9facd9-8b32-5537-b94e-bb833971bbbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a551105-1281-563b-9139-cdf718553556" :question/math-academy-id "q-91221" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left of ${a}_{44}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left of ${a}_{44}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-4){C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a477994-9c45-55b2-8144-b3659d076ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355191} {:answer/id #uuid "53f32427-b796-5beb-a84b-c128fa08761b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355410} {:answer/id #uuid "54c31c85-f366-5772-9219-7e9652a6a9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355416} {:answer/id #uuid "6b5679cc-5df2-5e8d-be56-472423bde4ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355613} {:answer/id #uuid "fb93e011-84ae-5f31-935d-2c2555d5038d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a477994-9c45-55b2-8144-b3659d076ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355191} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ee71f6d-313c-5faf-9cbb-6d25c54df71c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "15878489-f600-5d8d-a45e-e1a6680dcacf" :question/math-academy-id "q-91232" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left of ${a}_{44}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the left of ${a}_{44}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(49-25) \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
